<section class="legal-page bg-body text-body">
  <div class="container legal-page-container">
    <article class="legal-page-content rte">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated"><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 13, 2026</p>
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how {{ shop.name }} collects, uses, discloses, and protects personal information when you visit our website, contact us, subscribe to emails, or place an order.</p>

      <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Contact and order details, such as your name, email address, phone number, billing address, shipping address, and order history.</li>
        <li>Personalization details, such as photos, names, dates, messages, artwork, and production instructions you choose to submit.</li>
        <li>Communication information, including messages sent through our contact form, email, or social media.</li>
        <li>Technical and usage information, such as device type, browser, approximate location, IP address, pages viewed, and interactions with the store.</li>
        <li>Marketing preferences, including whether you subscribe to our gift ideas and offers emails.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use personal information to process and deliver orders, create personalized products, communicate about orders or questions, provide customer support, prevent fraud and misuse, improve our website and products, comply with legal obligations, and send marketing messages where permitted and consistent with your choices.</p>

      <h2>3. Legal bases where applicable</h2>
      <p>Where privacy law requires a legal basis, we may process information because it is necessary to perform a contract with you, because you have given consent, because we have a legitimate business interest that does not override your rights, or because processing is necessary to comply with law. You may withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</p>

      <h2>4. Email marketing</h2>
      <p>If you subscribe to “Get Gift Ideas and Offers,” we may use your email address to send product inspiration, promotions, and store updates. You can unsubscribe at any time by using the unsubscribe link in an email or contacting us. Transactional messages about an order or service may still be sent when necessary.</p>

      <h2>5. How information is shared</h2>
      <p>We may share information with service providers that help us operate the store, such as Shopify, payment processors, fulfillment and production partners, shipping carriers, email providers, analytics and security providers, and customer-support tools. These providers may access information only as needed to provide services to us.</p>
      <p>We may also disclose information to comply with law, respond to lawful requests, protect customers or our business, investigate fraud or security incidents, or support a merger, sale, or business reorganization. We do not sell your personal information for money. We do not use your submitted personalization photos for unrelated advertising without your permission.</p>

      <h2>6. Shopify and third-party services</h2>
      <p>Our store is powered by Shopify. Shopify and other providers may process information according to their own policies and service terms. Payment details are handled by the payment method you select at checkout. When you follow a link to Instagram, Facebook, or another third-party service, that service’s privacy policy applies to your activity there.</p>

      <h2>7. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>We and our service providers may use cookies, pixels, local storage, and similar technologies to keep the store working, remember preferences, understand traffic, measure marketing, and help protect the store. You can manage cookies through your browser and, where available, our privacy or cookie settings. Some features may not work correctly if necessary cookies are disabled.</p>

      <h2>8. Retention</h2>
      <p>We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Policy, including order fulfillment, accounting, customer support, dispute resolution, fraud prevention, legal compliance, and legitimate business records. Retention periods vary depending on the type of information and applicable requirements.</p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect personal information. No online transmission or storage system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

      <h2>10. Your privacy choices and rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, deletion of, or a copy of your personal information; object to or restrict certain processing; withdraw consent; or opt out of marketing. To make a request, contact us at <a href="mailto:{{ shop.email }}">{{ shop.email }}</a>. We may need to verify your identity before completing a request. You may also have the right to complain to a data-protection authority.</p>

      <h2>11. Children</h2>
      <p>Our store is not directed to children who are below the minimum age required to make purchases under applicable law. We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children for marketing purposes.</p>

      <h2>12. International transfers</h2>
      <p>Your information may be processed in countries other than the country where you live, including countries where Shopify or our service providers operate. Where required, we use appropriate safeguards for cross-border transfers.</p>

      <h2>13. Changes to this Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Policy when our practices, services, or legal obligations change. We will post the revised Policy on this page and update the effective date.</p>

      <h2>14. Contact us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions or privacy requests, contact us through our <a href="/pages/contact">Contact Us</a> page or email <a href="mailto:{{ shop.email }}">{{ shop.email }}</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Privacy Policy",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
